WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.460
Mom!

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:11.460
Riko!

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.010
Mom!

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.690
"Confusion"

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.070
What is it?

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.660
Is something wrong?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.620
Nothing at all.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.790
Riko!

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.170
Umm, Mom. The chopsticks...

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:17.420
Oh, sorry!

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.840
Now go wash your face!
I'm making breakfast!

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.680
'Kay!

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.770
Riko, being forced to wear this...

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:45.160
No! I absolutely... absolutely
refuse to let that happen!

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:51.750
Ouch...

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.170
What happened?!

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.840
I'm fine. I just slipped.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.920
You must be exhausted, Mom.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:03.890
You need to be careful,
since you do dangerous work!

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:06.180
I'm fine!

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.140
Dangerous work? How does Riko know that?

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.900
Tozawa!

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.780
You told Rihoko about me, didn't you?!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.990
What brought that on?
I was up late last night, y'know...

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.780
I'm talking about my work!

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.160
Huh?

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.710
Oh, now that you mention it,
I did tell her you fight X-Cons.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.000
You what?!

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:40.800
How could you do that?!
You promised to keep it a secret from her!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.390
Why did you tell her, you idiot?! Idiot! Idiot!

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.140
I-It's okay!

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.890
I didn't tell her that you transform!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.770
She probably thinks you're
like a cop or something.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.150
A cop?

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:04.740
Well, I guess that's alright. But...

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.200
Look. I'm sitting on a ton of stories here,

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.830
but I haven't gone public with
'em because of our agreement.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:16.420
So I'd appreciate it if you'd be grateful...

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.090
Of course I'm grateful. It was a promise.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:24.760
Anyway, at this point, I wanna
have the whole story blow open!

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.600
My target now is Father of the NSWF.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.560
He has his genes in all
of the Sisters, you know.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.520
Eh?!

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.730
That's not ordinary obsessiveness.
Don't you wanna know why?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:42.860
Nope.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.700
Doesn't matter to me, as long
as he stays away from Rihoko.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.450
And don't tell her anything else!

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.290
Rihoko, Rihoko, Rihoko, Rihoko...

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:59.330
Has she gotten even worse than before?

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:04.590
Success!

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:10.720
So, this document proves that you are Rihoko's mother?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:11.760
Yeah!

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:16.850
Though you two are clearly family,
even without this piece of paper!

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:21.860
Naomi-bou, can you foresee
what's in their future?

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:26.450
Did that Takayama fellow arrange this?

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.900
Yeah, probably.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.410
Oh? That was certainly nice of him...

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.040
W-What's that mean?!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.710
Here you go! Snack time!

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.330
They look great!

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.710
I humbly accept this!

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.300
You've gotten even better!

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.340
I'm going to give one to
the lady at the bathhouse!

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:53.430
Hold on! It's dangerous to go alone

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:54.680
Eh?!

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:57.020
I think going with you is more dangerous...

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:01.400
Stay out of this, Mariko-san!
This is a family issue!

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:02.980
Let's go, Riko!

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.690
Okay. But be careful.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:09.450
Masamune-Chan seems to
have become a worrywart...

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:12.030
That must be a burden on Rihoko,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.830
but someday they'll grow apart.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:17.410
Not good...

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.040
Huh?

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.500
My snack...

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.300
Chou-san! That's Naomi's snack!

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.470
Eh? It is?

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:34.890
You're terrible! Terrible!
Sorry, Naomi-bou! I'll give it back!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.730
Let's go to an amusement
park after we deliver this!

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.650
Eh? Really?!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.820
I hardly get the chance to go
places with you, so it'd be nice!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.110
Hurray!

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.530
"No Weapons for Baradhi!"
"Exporting Weapons is Unconstitutional!"
"No War"

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.330
There certainly are a lot of them.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.880
Though conflict naturally comes
with businesses dealing in weapons.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.220
Protestors are really hitting
us hard too, these days.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.930
It's nothing new. Have the PR
department deal with them.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:19.890
What's on today's schedule?

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:26.860
You're completely booked, because
of all your time with Masane-san.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:28.730
You appear to have a complaint.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.320
No, not at all.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:34.610
It's just that Wadou-san's project
seems to be progressing quite well,

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:37.280
so I was wondering if we
should really sit idly by...

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.330
I already told you he'll fail.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:44.920
That may be because you've
known Wadou-san since college,

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.420
but people do change.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.800
The tortoise did beat the hare, you know.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.760
Though calling you a hare is too cute.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.560
He's the hare who jumped the gun.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.970
That's pretty creepy, too.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:08.060
Baradhi military personnel have
inquired about the Witchblade Project.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:11.190
It seems leaking the information was worth it.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.700
They're considering purchasing
some with their current budget.

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:17.740
But only after verifying
the data of the final version.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.910
Not a problem. It's complete.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.870
In all aspects, its data surpasses
Takayama's I-Weapons'.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:27.580
The contract is as good as ours.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:31.050
Baradhi is Director
Takayama's client, you know.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.710
Are you sure about this?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.630
What they want is superior merchandise.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:39.010
It's only natural for them
to want stronger weapons.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:42.890
I will be unveiling the project
extravagantly at today's board meeting.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:46.810
Having possession of the Witchblade
but no results to show for it,

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.480
as well as losing his client, will
cause Takayama's stock to plummet.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.070
I can see him weeping now.

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:56.990
Paying that NSWF researcher
all that money was really worth it!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:58.620
Keep your mouth shut!

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.160
I-I apologize!

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:09.210
Her post-Cloneblade progress is excellent.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:13.840
Her numbers show no abnormalities.
Actually, all her data has improved!

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.720
We still need to wait for the test
results of her genetic-level changes,

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.130
but I have high hopes!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.100
I'd expect no less from
someone so carefully selected!

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:25.560
Okay, Maria! All done! You did great!

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:34.690
Chief Nishida, doesn't something
seem strange about Maria?

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.820
Her data has no abnormalities.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:40.490
No, I mean she's suddenly very quiet,

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:43.660
and her earlier selfishness
is completely gone.

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:46.330
Yes, now that you mention it...

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:50.880
Maria is maturing right now,
so she probably shed her childishness.

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:55.590
Her growing up will make it
much easier to conduct research.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:57.220
Yes...

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:03.640
But both she and the
Sisters are at their limit.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:05.930
Any more of this will have the same results.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:07.680
What do you mean?

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.270
Because we can only use Father's genes.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.860
Those were his instructions...

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.360
Perhaps he just wants to
create clones of himself?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.780
No. He could easily
make clones if he wanted to.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.040
I don't know why he's obsessed
with using his own genes,

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.460
but at this rate, research will hit a dead-end.

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:39.720
You were perfect. As a person,
as a scholar, as a father...

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:46.850
But you made one mistake.
Choosing the mother to have me...

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:55.730
My body will remain cursed
because of that woman...

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.780
...for as long as I live.

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:10.160
Furumizu Tatsuoki...

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.790
Man, what a history...

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:19.050
Raised as a real rich kid, plus
he's damn smart. Pretty disturbing.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:22.930
Oh? So his old man was
a prize-winning scientist, too...

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:26.390
If his mom turns out to be a hottie...

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:32.060
What's the deal?!
There's no info on his mom at all!

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:35.810
Yes, could I speak with the person in charge

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:39.610
of the biography of
Director Furumizu of the NSWF?

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.910
Why does this go into
extreme detail about his father,

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.830
but not mention his mother in the slightest?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:53.920
He claimed that his mother
didn't like to be in the public eye.

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:59.130
There was a single photo of his
mother among the photos he gave me.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.720
He probably forgot to dispose of it.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:06.010
I do recognize the background
of that photo, though...

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.610
Yummy!

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:24.070
Today's like Christmas and New Year's
and my birthday all at once!

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.700
I'm having fun, too! What should we do next?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.910
We can do anything you want, Riko!

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.660
Hmm... then... that!

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.920
That?

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:43.840
It's dark! And scary! I can't see anything!

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:47.220
Mom, that's because you have your eyes shut.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:54.230
T-They're kinda cute...

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.890
See?

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:03.230
Even they scare you, Mom?

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:06.740
There, there! It's okay, Mom!

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:17.830
This's definitely the place in that photo...

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:20.380
She really live in a place like this?

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:26.970
Excuse me. I'd like to ask you
about a long time ago; that okay?

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:32.220
You sayin' I look old enough
to know stuff from long ago?!

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:35.810
No, uhh, I didn't mean

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:39.100
Darling! Someone's tryin' to pick me up!

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:40.150
Eh?!

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.860
What, honey?

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.730
Oh, uhh... Hi.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.910
Get lost!

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:55.200
Takayama, it's been a while.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.870
Has it?

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:02.540
I just know you'll love my
announcement at today's meeting.

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:04.460
I can't wait.

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:07.550
Yes, look forward to it.

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:11.890
This confidence... Things might
be looking bad for the director...

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.430
In which case...

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.060
Dust.
Thank you.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:17.640
Not at all!

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:26.900
Wadou-kun's Bio-Section has a report
today, so let us begin with that.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:31.870
Thank you. Please have a look at your monitors.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:38.620
I present to you the result of
the Bio-Section's Witchblade Project,

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:41.420
the Ultimate Blade!

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:44.000
Director Takayama can
surely surmise what it does.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:48.630
Indeed, this is a Witchblade
that even men can wear.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.220
Is this true?!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:54.800
Yes. The specs are right here.
I'll explain it simply.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:58.060
The Joule-Heat Armor is
powered by body electricity

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:01.140
and has a mass efficiency
of 4.5 with KE shells,

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:04.020
and is theoretically capable of
withstanding tungsten shells.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:06.520
As a result of the
metallomics mixture filament,

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:10.280
reaction velocity and acceleration
are over 4 times that of I-Weapons.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:11.910
That's basically it.

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.320
Takayama-kun...

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:17.950
...you're an expert weapon developer;
I'd love to hear your thoughts.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.750
Your honest opinion will do fine.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:25.500
Yes. It probably is the most
powerful weapon I've ever seen.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.590
What an honor it is to hear that from you...

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:36.010
However, this runs the risk of
turning its very wearers into weapons.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.890
So what? That's the entire point!

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:44.650
According to our forecasts,
exports of the Ultimate Blade

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:48.270
will increase sales 1 50% over last year.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:53.200
That's wonderful, but our client
countries don't have limitless budgets.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.740
I take issue with your encroachment
upon Takayama-kun's territory.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.160
It couldn't be helped.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:04.000
In fact, Baradhi has already made
inquiries about the Ultimate Blade.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.340
Takayama-kun, I know
they're your client, but...

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:08.840
No, go right ahead.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:11.170
Thank you, Takayama-kun.

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:14.470
Except... your forecast is wrong.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.590
What?!

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.050
It would be best to sell only one or two.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.100
Takayama! You're embarrassing yourself!

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.850
You're the one who attested
to the Ultimate's abilities!

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:28.860
This is an order form I just received
from Baradhi for more I-Weapons.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.820
W-What?!

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:33.780
You don't mean... Baradhi
wasn't planning to buy Ultimates?!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:36.780
They did say they were merely considering it.

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:41.700
Wadou-san, have you even
been to a battlefield before?

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:45.500
What is wanted on the battlefield
now is not devastating power,

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:49.920
but precise weapons that
result in minimal loss of life.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.920
Unfortunately, the Ultimate lacks that!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.380
What?!

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:58.680
Cost performance-wise, they're
many times inferior to I-Weapons.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:04.180
We're not dealing with
weapon aficionados here.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:07.850
You've done nothing more
than play games on paper.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:15.740
Well done, sir! It turned out
that he had let his guard down!

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:18.870
Oh, dust!

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.700
Boy, am I glad I didn't switch sides...

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:31.420
Takayama... You'll pay for this!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:41.430
Yagi...

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:43.600
Yagi!

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:49.850
You must really be exhausted, Riko.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.740
Yes?

00:17:57.610 --> 00:17:59.070
What happened to you?!

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:02.240
I found out about Father.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:07.160
Father hates his mother.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.920
His mother?

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:13.420
His father was a top scientist for the NSWF,

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:17.300
but when he was still in school,
he fell in love and had a kid.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.220
And that was Father?

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:24.640
Yep. But not only was he a student,
the Furumizu family's really strict,

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:27.890
so it took 10 years to get
approval to marry the woman.

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:31.770
During that time, Father lived with his mother.

00:18:31.860 --> 00:18:36.190
That means she raised him!
Why would he hate her?

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:40.910
Apparently, she did business out
of her home the police didn't like.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.120
As a kid, he was probably embarrassed,

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:48.870
but it wasn't until after he grew up
that he started to really hate her.

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.410
What do you mean?

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:56.210
I found out that Father can't have kids.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:59.340
In his eyes, being even
slightly different from his father

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:01.840
would be the same as
being completely rejected.

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:05.430
So he blamed it entirely on his mother,

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:07.930
who was cheerful but had placed him

00:19:08.020 --> 00:19:12.560
in a bad environment for a while.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:18.820
Maria, someday, you will
become the perfect mother...

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:22.780
The perfect mother, created from my genes...

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:27.330
And the one borne from you will be the true me.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:30.040
My flawed self will disappear,

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:34.040
and my proper self will live
on and leave offspring...

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:39.800
Mother...

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:45.510
That's messed up!
Creating people for something like that!

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.810
I guess you could say it's
a type of mother complex.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:52.310
So-called "twisted love."
You better be careful, yourself.

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:53.810
Why me?

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:57.820
You've been over-obsessive with Rihoko lately.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:19:59.900
Don't compare me to him!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:04.860
I'm Riko's mother, you know!
What's wrong with holding her dear?!

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.670
Riko...

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.470
An X-Con?

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.020
It's gone now...

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:55.160
What?! But we recovered all
the X-Cons when we found Reina!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.710
But that's the only thing that
could do something this horrible!

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:02.880
What does this mean?

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:19.310
I-I'm sorry. Did I wake you?

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.820
Maria-sama?

00:21:23.860 --> 00:21:26.950
Crying and shouting is foolish.

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:29.530
No one will give us what we want.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.790
Our only choice is to obtain it ourselves.

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:37.290
And we have the power
to do that, we Neo-Genes...

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.960
No, we chosen ones...

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:54.740
I turn around half-asleep as my hits the right side of my cheek

00:21:54.740 --> 00:22:02.990
Your voice was there, and the air was warm

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:11.260
Your right hand grazes my left shoulder

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:15.730
But why don't you hold on tight?

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:28.500
In order to change yesterday's wish tomorrow,

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:35.690
I need to grow stronger myself

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:44.840
Even now, I am breathing in your scent, ...

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:53.510
and jumping over to your side. Give me your love.

00:22:55.180 --> 00:23:02.990
Extend your hands. Reach them out to me.

00:23:02.990 --> 00:23:09.540
I'm so happy

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:16.060
Riko, there's no need
to worry ever again!

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:20.770
l'm going to keep working lots,
and earn lots of money!

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:26.110
You'd be so shocked if you
saw how much we have saved up!

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:27.400
Wanna see?

00:23:27.480 --> 00:23:29.740
Too bad! It's still a secret!

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:33.110
Instead, I'll buy you lots of clothes!

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:35.830
And we can go anywhere you want!

00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:39.500
I'd do anything for you, Riko.
